Builds on the QuestTalkFixture PR (test fixture only).

Problem. Sheep Shearer (Fred the Farmer, north-west of Lumbridge) had no
quest script: Fred, The Thing and the hand-in were missing, and the
quest varp the client and Quest Helper read was never set.

Change.
- Progress is varp 179 (`varp.sheep`) as in OSRS: 0 not started, 1
  started, 1 + balls of wool handed in, 21 complete (checked against the
  cache dbrow's end state at startup). Rewards: 1 QP, 150 Crafting XP, 60
  coins.
- Fred's dialogue follows the wiki transcript: the three opening options,
  the offer and start prompt, shears from Fred when the player has none,
  the spinning help with the spinning wheel map icon box (obj
  crafting_icon_dummy, the transcript's pic 7670), the mid-quest count and
  the three help options, the unspun-wool reply.
- Hand-ins: partial deliveries ("You give Fred n balls of wool." / "I
  need n more before I can pay you."); the last delivery goes straight to
  "That's the last of them." without the give box. Only unnoted balls of
  wool count. If the reward cannot be given (coins already at the stack
  limit), the balls go back, the quest stays open and the player is told
  "You don't have enough room for the reward."
- Carrying 20 balls of wool when first asking for the quest: the "In fact
  Fred, funnily enough..." exchange comes right after "...the small matter
  of The Thing.", takes 20 balls and completes the quest, with no Thing
  exposition, start prompt or hand-in lines.
- The Thing (npc 731): Shear (op1) and shears used on it give "The...
  whatever it is... manages to get away from you!"; Talk-to (op3) is the
  player's "That's a sheep...I think. I can't talk to sheep." A shearing
  attempt sets a server varbit that gates "Fred! Fred! I've seen The
  Thing!" during and after the quest; after the quest without it Fred
  offers only kill / lost.

Tests. SheepShearerInteractionTest (9): accept (varp 1, shears, icon
box), decline, partial and final hand-in (varp 6 -> 21, no give box on the
last delivery, rewards once), a full coin stack keeps the last wool and
leaves the quest open (hand-in and first-talk paths), 20 balls on the
first talk (complete before The Thing and the prompt, 1 spare ball kept),
The Thing's Talk-to,
the after-quest Thing option only after a shearing attempt (shears used on
it), the in-quest Thing option.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Sheep Shearer, Transcript:Sheep Shearer,
Transcript:Fred the Farmer, Transcript:Sheep (penguins); Quest Helper
SheepShearer (varp 179 steps 1-20); cache: npc 731 ops (Shear, Talk-to),
obj 7670 crafting_icon_dummy.

Caveats.
- The journal texts (reworked in OSRS on 14 January 2026) are best
  guesses.
- Shearing The Thing without shears uses OpenRune's sheep message "You
  need a set of shears to do this."; the OSRS line is not documented.
- "How do I shear sheep, again?" without shears hands over a new pair
  (the transcript shows Fred's line but no give box there).
- "Interacted with the Thing" is taken as a shearing attempt (Shear or
  shears used on it); Talk-to does not unlock the Fred option.
- "You don't have enough room for the reward." (reward does not fit) is
  a guess.
- Chathead expressions are best guesses.

